	(text "To avoid overheating problem with original regulator design, we decided to do 2 things:\n1) Lessen the change in voltage the regulator has to handle\n2) Separate the circuit into three busses (MCU, Sensors, and XB Radio) and make an individual regulator chain for each.\nBoth steps are pretty simple: For step 1, we decided to split the step-down into two parts: 7.4V-5V, 5V-3.3V. Originally \nthe regulator was going straight from 7.4 to 3.3, which would have the regulator dissipating 4W, which is way too much heat\nfor the little guy. For the second step, we will be splitting the current load so each regulator doesn't have to deal with the full might of the \ncircuit. Each bus will include a step down from 7.4 to 5, and then another step from 5 to 3.3. This should deal with our overheating issue.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.606 140.716 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f955fc4e-43ef-4def-bb5a-c220439606fe")
	)
	(text "Since a battery is our main source of power, an input capacitor is used on each LDO in order to \ngive it a smooth input voltage. To make sure the output is also smooth, each regulator also has an input cap.\n1uF decided by datasheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
